# WORKFLOW_DO_NOT_COMMIT
Purpose:
This is a developer-only placeholder describing the exact CI commands reviewers and maintainers should run. Do NOT convert this note into a GitHub Actions workflow or any other CI workflow file unless explicitly requested by the team. This file documents the commands the CI must run so local verification matches CI behavior.

Required CI commands (run in repository root):
1) Install dependencies (reproducible install)
   npm ci

2) Build production bundle
   npm run build

3) Run unit/component tests
   npm run test
   - Ensure test runner is configured to run in CI (headless, single-run).
   - For Vitest/Jest: use CI-friendly reporters; fail on coverage if configured.

4) Run end-to-end tests (Playwright)
   npm run test:e2e
   - Ensure Playwright browsers are installed before running: npx playwright install --with-deps
   - CI should run Playwright in headless mode and capture artifacts (screenshots, traces) into docs/evidence/ or a designated artifacts folder.

Recommended environment and notes:
- Node: use the project's supported Node version (check .nvmrc or engines in package.json). If unspecified, use Node 18+.
- PORT: apps that start a dev or test server must respect dynamic PORT assignment via:
   int(process.env.PORT || 5000)  (or equivalent). CI should not assume a fixed port.
- For reproducible builds, CI should set CI=true and install with npm ci.
- If additional steps are required (browser installation for Playwright, DB emulators, etc.), document them in the PR description and include install commands in CI job steps.

Why this file exists:
- Keeps reviewer checklist and exact local commands colocated with the repo.
- Prevents accidental creation of workflows that diverge from local test/build commands.
- Serves as the canonical developer reminder for what CI must run for each PR relating to the frontend.

If you are preparing a CI workflow, consult the team (maintainers) before converting these commands into .github/workflows/* so the project CI policy, secrets, and artifact storage are handled correctly.